# A time-travel move keeps both boards in view; the Submit after it focuses the one board Black must move on.
# Standard: 1. e4 e5, then the knight g1 on the present board jumps back to g3 on the first board (a new timeline, L+1).
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,250); Standard row (905,224); Play (808,712); Submit (841,90).
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 905 224        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 30
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 30
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 60
clicksq 0 1 e7
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 e5
wait 30
click 841 90
wait 60
camexpect state Focus
camexpect visible 0 2
clicksq 0 2 g1       # the white knight on the present board
wait 40
capture camera-timetravel-selected
clicksq 0 0 g3       # its target two half-turns back: it creates timeline L+1 (board L+1 T1b)
wait 60
camexpect visible 0 2   # the board it left ...
camexpect visible 1 1   # ... and the board it created
camexpect zoom 0.79 1.26
capture camera-timetravel-both-in-view
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 90
camexpect state Focus
camexpect visible 1 1   # Black's one mandatory board
camexpect zoom 0.79 1.26
capture camera-timetravel-submitted
